  "parent": {
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What your child is learning",
        "text": "To multiply by 3 using facts they already know: decompose 3 into 2 and 1. The 2s fact is a double; the 1s fact is the number itself. Add them. When the 3 comes second (8 × 3), decompose the 3 between the columns, or turn the fact around."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Try it with real things",
        "list": [
          "Make 3 rows of 8 coins. Cover the bottom row: 2 rows is 16. Uncover it: 16 + 8 = 24."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Questions to ask",
        "list": [
          "Where is the 3?",
          "What is the 2s fact?",
          "What is the 1s fact?"
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Common mistakes",
        "list": [
          "Doubling the 3 when it comes second: 8 × 3 answered as 9.",
          "Stopping at the double: 14 for 3 × 7.",
          "Adding 3 instead of the number: 19 for 3 × 8.",
          "Losing count when skip counting by 3s."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "A note on the book",
        "text": "The class book calls the two parts the \"2s fact\" and the \"1s fact\". Study Scoop uses original practice questions; it never copies the textbook."
      }
    ]
  }
